=== 8. crate-hub ===

* (HIGH) Container data path is dead end-to-end. crated's
  GET /api/v1/containers (daemon/routes.cpp:134-138) returns
  {"status":"ok","data":<jls --libxo json>} — an OBJECT; the hub
  stores the whole envelope as status.containers (hub/poller.cpp
  :143). AggregatorPure::countTopLevelObjects (aggregator_pure.cpp
  :40) requires [...] and returns 0, so /api/v1/aggregate,
  /api/v1/datacenters and /api/v1/scheduling/least-loaded
  (hub/api.cpp:116,135,201) always see 0 containers on every node
  (scheduler always a pure tie, confidence 50); /api/v1/containers
  (api.cpp:74) embeds the envelope and hub/web/app.js:124 then
  JSON.parse()s an already-parsed object → throws → "No containers"
  forever. tests/unit/hub_aggregator_pure_test.cpp:75-99 feeds only
  synthetic [{...}]. Fix on the hub side: unwrap data and
  jail-information.jail.

* (HIGH) Daemonised crate-hub never polls: hub/main.cpp:210 starts
  the poller thread, then :220 fork()s; the child has only the forking
  thread, so no poll loop runs in the default (non -f) mode. At
  shutdown :239 pollerThread.join() in the child joins a thread that
  does not exist in that process (std::system_error / UB). Fork
  before starting threads.

* (HIGH) Dashboard action buttons target the wrong host:
  hub/web/app.js:168-172 take the node host from cells[1] of the Nodes
  table, but since the Datacenter column was inserted (index.html:42,
  app.js:88-92) cells[1] is the datacenter → every
  start/stop/restart/destroy goes to https://default/... app.js:49,52
  also hard-code https:// while crated's TCP listener and the hub's
  own polling are plain HTTP by default, and crated emits no CORS
  headers (grep Access-Control in daemon/: none) — so the cross-origin
  fetch would be blocked anyway. Route actions through the hub.

* (MED) Hub API fully unauthenticated, bound to 0.0.0.0
  (hub/main.cpp:230), undocumented as such: no auth middleware in
  hub/api.cpp; POST /api/v1/admin/prune (api.cpp:213) deletes data and
  is CSRF-able from any website; crate-hub.8 has no
  AUTHENTICATION/SECURITY section; /api/v1/nodes leaks node host:port
  and error strings.

* (MED) Node polling has no server-cert verification path and sends
  tokens in cleartext by default: hub/poller.cpp:112-117 uses TLS only
  when tls_cert (a CLIENT cert) is configured; no set_ca_cert_path /
  enable_server_certificate_verification, so an HTTPS crated with a
  server-only cert cannot be polled, and the default path sends the
  admin Bearer token (:122) over plain HTTP. poller.cpp also never
  defines CPPHTTPLIB_OPENSSL_SUPPORT (daemon/server.cpp:10 does), so
  httplib::SSLClient at :113 will not compile once a hub build target
  exists.

* (MED) Hand-built JSON with unescaped interpolation:
  hub/api.cpp:33-37,55,74,98 splice s.name, s.host, s.lastError and
  the raw node body into JSON/Prometheus output (JsonPure is used by
  ha/scheduling but not here). One node answering 200 with a non-JSON
  body (reverse-proxy error page) makes /api/v1/containers invalid
  JSON for the whole cluster.

* (MED) crate-hub.8 CONFIGURATION contradicts the code: man :81-94
  documents listen_port, separate host:/port: keys and
  --foreground/--config; the code reads only `host` as host:port
  (poller.cpp:52,106-108, default 9800), ignores `port` and
  `listen_port` (port only via -p, main.cpp:177), accepts only short
  flags (:175-178). Omits datacenter, tls_cert/tls_key, ha:,
  /api/v1/datacenters, /api/v1/ha/orders,
  /api/v1/scheduling/least-loaded and the `schedule` subcommand.

* (MED) Poller writes shared state outside the mutex:
  poller.cpp:146,149 touch status.lastError / hostInfo / containers
  without statusMutex_ while getNodeStatuses() (:160-163) copies under
  it → data race on std::string. On a down node `containers` keeps the
  last good body and recordPoll (:149) still inserts it each cycle →
  stale data presented as fresh with no flag.

* (MED) IPv6 node hosts cannot be configured: poller.cpp:106-108
  splits on the last `:` → [::1]:9800 yields host "[::1]" and bare
  ::1 yields host ":" + port 1; stoi failures mark the node
  permanently down with lastError="stoi".

* (LOW) /api/v1/nodes omits `datacenter` (api.cpp:33-38) so the Nodes
  table always shows "default" (app.js:91). main.cpp:177 stoi on -p
  uncaught; :206 SQLite open throws if /var/db/crate-hub/ is absent
  (nothing creates it); :229-231 listen() failure is silent and main
  sleeps forever. store.cpp: one sqlite3* shared by poller and HTTP
  threads with no mutex (safe only with SQLITE_THREADSAFE=1 —
  plausible). poller.cpp:51 n["host"].as<string>() throws on a node
  without `host` and silently drops all later nodes; :125,140 a down
  node costs two 5 s timeouts so N down nodes exceed poll_interval.
  api.cpp:164 emits HA failover orders from the hub's own view only
  (hub-side partition → orders while the primary is healthy;
  mitigated because `crate migrate` needs the source).

=== 9. crate-snmpd ===

* (HIGH) Spins at 100% CPU and never reconnects after the master
  closes the socket: snmpd/mib.cpp:410-414 — on EOF select() is
  readable immediately, readN returns 0, dispatchOnce returns false,
  the main loop (snmpd/main.cpp:84-93) calls it again with no delay;
  g_agentxFd stays >= 0, no reconnect/backoff exists. A
  bsnmpd/snmpd restart permanently kills monitoring and pins a core.

* (HIGH) AgentX session ID never taken from the Open response:
  mib.cpp:221-223 sets g_sessionId = g_transactionId (=1) instead of
  header bytes 4-7 of the Response. Register/Close then carry a
  sessionId the master did not assign → RFC 2741 §7.1.1 notOpen;
  registration fails with any master that does not hand out 1
  (plausible); protocol violation confirmed; only logged (:255).

* (MED) OctetString length overflow → out-of-bounds read:
  mib_pure.cpp:116-119 — n is uint32_t, (n + 3) wraps for
  n >= 0xFFFFFFFD → padded = 0 → bounds check passes → out.assign(ptr,
  n) reads ~4 GB past the buffer. Reachable via the
  NON_DEFAULT_CONTEXT string (:145-148). mib.cpp:420 and :151 also
  allocate payloadLen bytes with no cap (bad_alloc uncaught). Requires
  a hostile/buggy master on the local socket.

* (MED) Little-endian flag honoured only in the header:
  mib_pure.cpp:83-88 flips header fields, but decodeOid (:108) and
  decodeOctetString (:116) always use loadU32be; mib_pure.h:78-79
  claims LE is handled.

* (MED) CRATE-MIB table and traps are not implemented but documented
  as the product: mib.cpp:371-374 answers noSuchInstance for every
  non-scalar OID; resolveGetNext (:380-387) walks only 4 scalars;
  sendTrap (:316-319) only logs. snmpd/CRATE-MIB.txt:65-165 defines an
  11-column table plus NOTIFICATION-TYPEs; README.md:761-763 says the
  agent "exposes container metrics". collector.h:20 says "CPU% x 100"
  but collector.cpp:52 stores raw percent; netRx/netTx/uptimeTicks
  never populated.

* (LOW) mib.cpp:263-287 registers root + two overlapping child
  subtrees at equal priority (duplicateRegistration, logged only);
  :430-437 answers Response PDUs with a Response; :449 write() return
  unchecked and SIGPIPE not ignored; :139,152 short read() not looped.
  mib.cpp:90 g_version = "0.8.48" and port/Makefile:2
  PORTVERSION=0.8.48 vs 1.1.33 (cli/args.cpp:756). main.cpp:41-48
  `-i 0` runs jls/rctl every 100 ms.

=== 10. Carried over from the previous TODO (still open, unchanged) ===

* (correctness, FreeBSD-only) lib/run.cpp exception-path teardown
  order diverges from the success path: the happy path tears down in
  an explicit doNow() order (jail → mounts → net → fw-slot,
  ~:1942-1984); on a throw before that block, RunAtEnd destructors
  fire in reverse-declaration order — network teardowns (~:1051-1068)
  run BEFORE destroyJail (:958), mounts unmount last, removeMacRules
  (:669) runs against an already-recycled jid. Cleanup quality on an
  already-failing run. Fix: one ordered teardown for both paths.
  Validate on a real FreeBSD host (docs/on-hardware-validation.md).

* (correctness, MED) lib/run.cpp registers several teardown handlers
  AFTER the operations that can throw: NetworkLease::allocateFor
  succeeds (~:1153) but configureStaticIp/copyFile throws before
  releaseLeaseAtEnd is set → lease row stays forever (see also 3.
  "leases never reclaimed"); same for IPv6 (~:1184); bridge
  auto-created (~:1090) then setUp/createBridgeEpair throws before
  destroyBridgeEpairAtEnd.reset (~:1115) → bridge + epair leak;
  run_net.cpp createBridgeEpair / the extras loop (~:1664) leak an
  epairN pair per failed attempt. Register the RunAtEnd immediately
  after each successful acquisition.

* (correctness/security, MED) lib/network_lease.cpp +
  network_lease6.cpp flock the lease FILE's inode but writeAllAtomic
  renames a fresh inode over the path → a second waiter holds a lock
  on the unlinked inode and reads stale contents → two concurrent
  `crate run` by the same user allocate the SAME address. Same bug in
  spec_registry.cpp (section 5). Fix with a stable `<path>.lock`.

  [FIXED in 1.1.36] jid→owner registry forget-by-name: destroy_jail
  now resolves name→jid before the handler runs and forgets by jid;
  stale rows are reconciled against live jails.

* (correctness, MED) lib/stack.cpp `stack up` calls runCrate()
  IN-PROCESS and sequentially per container (stack.cpp:871,977): a
  service-only first container never returns, so the second is never
  started. Spawn each `crate run` like daemon/routes.cpp spawnCrateRun.

  [FIXED in 1.1.37] fd hygiene part 2: accept4(SOCK_CLOEXEC) on the
  three hand-rolled listeners, FD_CLOEXEC on the httplib listening
  sockets via set_socket_options.

* (correctness, MED) cron: all entries go into ONE crontab,
  /var/cron/tabs/<user of the FIRST entry> (run.cpp:1823); a `user:`
  on a later entry is silently ignored. Documented as a limitation in
  crate.5 (1.1.31). Group by user, one crontab per user.

  [FIXED in 1.1.37] connection-fd recv/send timeouts and a per-listener
  concurrency cap on the privops and control-socket planes.

* (correctness, LOW) lib/privops_wire_pure.cpp escape() is the one
  JSON escaper not on JsonPure: passes control bytes through raw. Its
  decoder (~:60) lacks \uXXXX, so teach the decoder first (round-trip
  test), then delegate.

* (LOW batch) daemon/routes.cpp:1014 import tmp file
  <name>.crate.tmp.<pid> is constant across threads (two concurrent
  imports of one name interleave; no fsync before rename);
  execPipelineImpl fork() failure for child i>0 throws without
  reaping children 0..i-1; capture loops treat read()==-1 as EOF
  (EINTR); jail_query.cpp ignores waitpid failure / decodes an
  uninitialised status; ws_console.cpp select() with fds >= FD_SETSIZE;
  run.cpp hcThread joinable while execInJail can throw on fork EAGAIN
  → std::terminate skips every RunAtEnd; stack.cpp inet_pton results
  unchecked for ip_range.

* (consistency, LOW) hub/ha_pure isValidName caps names at 64; switch
  to NameLimits::kJailName when the hub gets a build target.

* (security, HIGH-if-reachable, latent) libvirt VM track
  (lib/vm_spec.cpp:97-184 generateDomainXml embeds name / disk /
  bridge / hostPath / tag unescaped into domain XML handed to
  virDomainCreateXML as root; vm_run.cpp:250-388 and vm_stack.cpp:88
  build root-written paths from vmName / vol.tag with no traversal or
  newline check; memoryToKiB val*1024*1024 overflow). No caller
  today (built only WITH_LIBVIRT). Decision 2026-10: kept as roadmap.
  XML-escape / validate every field BEFORE wiring it up.

